{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WNnUpXJShAoWhDEmksZvGZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each \"planned\" experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"best\" tier assumptions. Let me identify the planned experiments:\n\n1. **gold-set** (status: planned) - Human-annotated 650 windows — GO/NO-GO gate\n\nAnd from the **what_if** section (these are hypothetical/additive experiments that are part of the D053 补缺实验):\n2. **llm-judge-fewshot** - LLM-as-judge few-shot + CoT variant\n\n\n3. **structural-feature-overlap-ablation** - Remove LF-overlapping features from structural vector\n4. **cross-agent-instance-isolation** - Re-evaluate cross-agent structural GB under instance-level isolation\n\nThe \"best\" tier definition says:\n- Gold-MV agreement ≥90%\n- Structural on gold still far ahead of probe\n- Overlap ablation residual F1 ≥0.85\n- LLM-judge few-shot still ≤0.75\n- Cross-agent instance isolation GB ≥0.95\n- gold_kappa: [0.78, 0.85]\n\nNow I'm looking at the expected performance ranges for each of these metrics to validate the tier definition.\n\nI need to lay out the predicted results for each experiment with clear reasoning. For the gold-set experiment specifically, I'm working with the simulated results from the dryrun on 650 windows where majority vote serves as a proxy for ground truth. In the best tier, I'm assuming human annotators achieve a kappa between 0.78-0.85 with 90-95% agreement against the majority vote labels.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38438,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38438},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"ses